# All optional. Copy to .env.local.

# mainnet (4663, default) or testnet (46630)
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN=mainnet

# The public RPC (https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com) is rate-limited.
# Use a provider URL for real traffic. It is shipped to browsers, so use a
# domain-restricted key.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL=

# Absolute site URL for metadata and OG images
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://example.com

# ---- Credits: pay by transfer (server-only; never prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_) ----
# Payments stay off unless PAYMENTS_ENABLED=1 and every setting below checks out. The server logs
# exactly what's wrong at startup. In production NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL is required too: sign-in is
# bound to its host.
# PAYMENTS_ENABLED=1

# Where deposits go. Use a Safe multisig: lenders are paid by hand from it.
# TREASURY_ADDRESS=0x...

# Signs session cookies. At least 32 bytes (openssl rand -hex 32). Changing it signs everyone out.
# SESSION_SECRET=

# The ledger is Postgres. On Vercel, and anywhere else that runs more than one instance, point
# DATABASE_URL at a database of its own: Neon from the Vercel Marketplace sets it (POSTGRES_URL works
# too). Use the pooled URL. Payments refuse to switch on on Vercel without it.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require

# Without DATABASE_URL the ledger is PGlite (Postgres in WebAssembly) kept in this directory: for
# local development, and for the single-instance Docker image (/data/ledger, on the /data volume).
# INFERNO_DB_PATH=.data/ledger

# Production never creates a new ledger by itself: an empty database means the wrong DATABASE_URL,
# an unmounted volume or a second copy, and a fresh ledger would credit every deposit again. Payments
# stay off and the log says "No ledger in ...". Set this for the very first start only, then remove it.
# INFERNO_DB_INIT=1

# Lets the scheduler call GET /api/cron/deposits (every 5 minutes), which samples $INFERNOAI's price,
# credits final deposits and settles Bittensor answers that died half-way. Vercel Cron (vercel.json) sends it as `Authorization: Bearer <secret>`.
# Unset, that route answers 503. openssl rand -hex 32
# CRON_SECRET=

# Server-only RPC for the deposit indexer and sign-in checks. Its key never reaches browsers, so
# visitors can't burn its quota. Unset: NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL (or the public RPC) is used.
# RPC_URL=

# Wallets that can download unpaid lender earnings and record payouts, comma-separated. The treasury
# Safe is shared, so their transfers to it are treasury funding: recorded, never credited.
# ADMIN_ADDRESSES=

# Each transfer credits at most this many dollars; the rest is recorded for a manual review.
# MAX_CREDIT_USD_PER_DEPOSIT=500

# Each wallet's transfers credit at most this many dollars in any 24 hours; the rest is recorded
# for a manual review, like the per-transfer cap.
# MAX_CREDIT_USD_PER_DAY=200

# First block to scan on a fresh ledger: the block the treasury was announced, not earlier. The
# chain makes about 10 blocks a second and each 2,000 blocks is one RPC call, so a far-back start
# takes hours to catch up. Default: the finalized block at first start. Ignored once the ledger
# has a cursor.
# DEPOSIT_START_BLOCK=

# USDG is always accepted, at $1, and on mainnet $INFERNOAI at its live price from its Uniswap pool,
# sampled by the cron every 5 minutes (docs/deploy.md). TAO and another coin are accepted at manual
# prices only with ALLOW_MANUAL_PRICES=1; without it they're ignored (the log says so).
# RISK: if a manual price is above market, anyone can buy the token cheap, deposit it for credits,
# spend them on "network answers" from a lender wallet they also run, and be paid out in USDG.
# The caps above limit it. Before every payout, open the earnings CSV and check `askers`: a lender
# paid mostly by one wallet is what this looks like.
# ALLOW_MANUAL_PRICES=1

# Accept TAO at this manual USD price (mainnet only; restart to change it).
# TAO_USD_PRICE=

# Accept another coin (such as one on testnet) at this manual USD price. Symbol and decimals are
# read from the chain. $INFERNOAI needs neither: it's priced live.
# COIN_ADDRESS=
# COIN_USD_PRICE=

# ---- Hosting (docs/deploy.md) ----
# Redis for the network relay, so any number of instances share lenders, streams and inboxes.
# Vercel's Upstash integration sets KV_URL, read when REDIS_URL is unset. Unset both: the relay
# lives in this server's memory (one long-running instance only); on Vercel it stays off (503).
# REDIS_URL=rediss://default:<password>@<host>.upstash.io:6379

# Behind a proxy (Railway, Render, Fly, Caddy, nginx), trust its client-IP header so rate limits are
# per visitor. Without it every visitor shares one set of limits. Automatic on Vercel.
# TRUST_PROXY=1
# Fly.io only: its x-forwarded-for can be prefixed by the client, so read Fly's own header instead.
# CLIENT_IP_HEADER=fly-client-ip

# ---- Bittensor (Chutes, subnet 64) ----
# Server key used when people pay for Bittensor answers with Inferno credits. People who bring their
# own Chutes key don't need this. Never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# CHUTES_API_KEY=
